ext\" href=\"https://developer.amd.com/amd-aocc/\">developer<wbr />.amd<wbr />.com<wbr />/amd-aocc<wbr />/</a></span></td></tr></tbody></table> \n<p>The <b>AMD Optimizing C/C++ Compiler</b> (<b>AOCC</b>) is an optimizing C/C++ and Fortran <a href=\"/wiki/Compiler\" title=\"Compiler\">compiler</a> suite from <a href=\"/wiki/AMD\" title=\"AMD\">AMD</a> targeting 32-bit and 64-bit <a href=\"/wiki/Linux\" title=\"Linux\">Linux</a> platforms.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-userguide&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-userguide-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-larabel2&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-larabel2-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> It is a proprietary fork of <a href=\"/wiki/LLVM\" title=\"LLVM\">LLVM</a> + <a href=\"/wiki/Clang\" title=\"Clang\">Clang</a>  with various additional patches to improve performance for AMD's <a href=\"/wiki/Zen_(microarchitecture)\" title=\"Zen (microarchitecture)\">Zen</a> microarchitecture in <a href=\"/wiki/Epyc\" title=\"Epyc\">Epyc</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Ryzen\" title=\"Ryzen\">Ryzen</a> microprocessors.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-userguide&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-userguide-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-larabel&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-larabel-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-userguide-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-userguide_1-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-userguide_1-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-ou